---@class save A save file being read or written. The same visitor function does both: `wallet = s:ints('wallet', wallet)` loads the value when reading and stores it when writing.

---@class city The building meta-game: ground, zones, a catalogue of building types and the placed buildings. Fields read and write the engine's state; struct-valued fields are copied, so `local cam = c.cam; cam.view = r; c.cam = cam`. Callbacks receive the city as their first argument.
---@field ground texture Loaded by init.
---@field defs building_def[] The building catalogue; assign a sequence.
---@field items building[] The placed buildings.
---@field count integer How many buildings are placed.
---@field zones city_zone[]
---@field zone_count integer
---@field open integer Bit per opened zone (bit 0 = zone 0, which starts open).
---@field spacing number Minimum distance between buildings without footprints.
---@field tile number A tile's side on the ground in world units; defaults to 45. Set it before init: building sizes are in tiles, projected by the engine's city camera.
---@field clearance size2 Tiles added to every sized footprint (w, h), so bases keep apart: size2(1, 1) leaves half a tile of ground on each side. Sprites keep their size.
---@field buildable function function(c, world) -> bool: terrain test.
---@field zone_at function function(c, world) -> zone (0-based) or -1; default: zone rects.
---@field zone_touches function function(c, zone, open) -> bool: adjacency; default: rects touching.
---@field draw_over function function(c): game drawing above the fog and buildings, below the ghost.
---@field cam camera
---@field fog color Locked zones; default dark teal.
---@field fog_on_land_only boolean
---@field fog_clouds boolean Animated world-space cloud density and billow lighting, clipped to the closed-region mask.
---@field path color Paths linking buildings; alpha 0 = none.
---@field movable boolean Hold a building still for 0.5 seconds to pick it up; ordinary drags pan the map.
---@field show_footprints boolean Debug: draw every building's footprint and pivot over its sprite, to check the sprite's measurements.
---@field income_icon texture
---@field selected integer Quick build: a tap places this type at once (-1 = off).
---@field placing integer Building type being placed, -1 = none.
---@field moving integer Index being moved, -1 = a new building.
---@field ghost vec2 Where it would go.
---@field held boolean The ghost is being dragged: lifted over the footprint of the tile it will land on.

